newbie.. by Phil G. Fraering@srl03.c 
> But the start of the game is much harder than the middle and end.

Most of the difficulty comes from things that are immediately deadly. 
Sure, we've all got horror storeis about succumbing to hordes of orcs or
going down to a swarm of killer bees, but most of the deaths in the
upper levels tend to be instant things that a pet would not have helped
with.  Gnomes with wands, having a gnome hop onto a polymorph trap and
become a jabberwock, walking onto a dart trap and getting hit with a
dart that had deadly poison on it...that sort of thing.  Fido would not
have made a difference in any of these cases.  I'm not saying that pets
should be removed from the game...far from it.  Lots of people like to
play with them.  That's fine.  I'm just saying that the effort gone into
improving the game should be towards making the end more interesting and
difficult.  I think the first part of the game is balanced great...it is
interesting and fun, and it is difficult enough that it's an
accomplishment to get a character rolling.

I do wish there were a boolean option you could set as to whether you
wanted a pet to start out with or not.  I just don't like them much.  I
don't get much enjoyment from my pet saving me because it feels like it
isn't my character being successful (plus, can you imagine how
embarassed, say, a barbarian would be to admit that a kitten saved his
life?), and I don't like competing for corpses and experience.  That's
just my choice.

